WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.650
What does gate seven support?

2
00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:05.340
Each week's digest supports getting
advisories to the people who act,

3
00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:07.930
monitoring the providers,
and updating the risk

4
00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:11.037
assessment when the environment
changes significantly.

5
00:00:11.037 --> 00:00:16.227
The evidence chain supports continuous
monitoring and the protection of audit

6
00:00:16.227 --> 00:00:21.262
information: each record holds the time,
the environment, the change record, the

7
00:00:21.262 --> 00:00:23.354
command, the result, the controls,

8
00:00:23.354 --> 00:00:26.375
every file's hash, and the
previous record's hash.

9
00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:29.956
And the preflight's check that each
provider's notice contacts are

10
00:00:29.956 --> 00:00:33.862
named and current supports NIST's
control for notification agreements.

11
00:00:33.862 --> 00:00:35.475
Here's why the chain matters.

12
00:00:35.475 --> 00:00:40.212
In the workbook's lab, someone appends a
line to the digest after it was recorded.

13
00:00:40.212 --> 00:00:44.328
The next check fails twice: the file
no longer matches the hash list,

14
00:00:44.328 --> 00:00:46.499
and it no longer matches its record.

15
00:00:46.499 --> 00:00:50.230
Nobody can quietly edit the
evidence an assessor will read.
